{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for explicit state@3 request authoring (request 65fa914a) at exact head 21b7e74225885452ab0ad0dc49b33aaf2c326d54 on request/explicit-request-authoring, three commits over current main 183211c3 (21341300c, bb65d898, 21b7e742), fifty-two changed paths, no ui or embed change, fulfilling my promise 07a271e5. This head corrects changes-requested 1ca7b411 by planner on bb65d898 (which had corrected 4d3375f2 on 21341300c), on the same promise per the adopted repair-continuity rule. Second correction (1ca7b411): (1) legacy accepted retry through the public boundary: the reproduction gate is now idempotency key present plus request lifecycle or the reassign verb (mayReproduceAcceptedRequest), independent of the body; an accepted act is recovered by dedup identity before any ref is read, rebuilt under that act's own schema (state@0/@1/@2/@3 or reassign-if-unclaimed@0/@1, the table reproducibleRequestSchemas), the result-choice judgement is skipped only for schemas that state no result, and the rebuild is used only when byte-equal to the accepted signed act; a fresh key with no choice still refuses and changed intent under a reused key still refuses. Exercised through real CLI, MCP and resident POST /v0/act (TestCLI/MCP/ResidentRequestReplaysAnExistingLegacyAct) plus a legacy act whose body reads like a choice. (2) invalid replacement no longer drops the assignment: Workspace.PreflightGuardedReplacement runs the caller-known half of the replacement judgement (shape rules, reserved fields, resolveRequestChoice/ReadRequestChoice including branch shape and ref resolution) in gs reassign-if-unclaimed and MCP reassign_if_unclaimed before the retirement is appended; it recovers an accepted replacement under key/request first so resuming a landed pair still reads no ref; the same guardedReplacementBody runs again at signing, the two-act guard and its resumable race behaviour are unchanged, no new lifecycle, no silent target inheritance