refs/heads/side does not resolve', plus the app, resident and MCP counterparts and TestCLIRequestMeasuresTheRefAtEachFiling :317); recovering target_ref too (TestCLIReusedKeyWithADifferentDestinationIsRefused :527 'a reused key naming refs/heads/other was accepted', plus app, resident and MCP counterparts); byte-equality gate (internal/app TestReusedKeyWithADifferentDestinationIsRefused :198). I re-ran the first two whole-guard mutants myself in a separate detached worktree at this head with the same red lines. (1) every request-lifecycle state reaching app.buildActRequest is signed workroom/state@3 and must state exactly one result; the caller names target_ref, the boundary fills target_repo with the workroom genesis id and reads target_head from the ref with git show-ref --verify at filing; a caller-supplied target_repo or target_head is refused outright, distinct from a release report's target_pre_head, which is untouched. (2) The body-local half of the judgement is the exported workroom.ReadRequestChoice, which the fold's decideRequestResult now calls, so surfaces refuse exactly the shapes the fold refuses in the same words; the ancestry walk and roster read stay in the fold, and all existing fold refusal strings are preserved. Missing, mixed, malformed, foreign-repo, non-branch and unresolvable choices refuse before signing, so the frontier does not move. (3) One path serves gs state, gs batch entries, the MCP state tool and the resident POST /v0/act. The guarded reassign-if-unclaimed replacement is filed under the new workroom/reassign-if-unclaimed@1 and states its own result; nothing is inherited from the retired request, so gs reassign-if-unclaimed gains --body and the MCP tool gains body. (4) kernel.PriorAct returns the act already accepted under an actor's idempotency key from the dedup index Submit consults; reproduceAcceptedTarget rebuilds the request from that act's own triple and uses it only when byte-identical to the accepted signed intent, so an exact retry after the ref moved replays and a fresh key measures the current ref; no new state machine or retry cache. (5) state@2 and reassign-if-unclaimed@0 bytes and interpretation are unchanged; an exact retry of an accepted state@2 request replays it. (6) Producer inventory in docs/reference/gs/state.md: gs state, gs batch, MCP state, resident /v0/act sign state@3; reassign-if-unclaimed signs @1; gs review, gs merge and cmd/gitseq-github produce no request; the perfscenario fixture states no_git_artifact=true. The cmd/gs merge fixture files its implementation request deliberately as state@2 through submitLegacyState because the phase-one authorization tests are about the legacy window; docs/reference/gs/merge.md now files its example implementation request as landing=held with target_repo/target_ref on the release. The I5 input/output contract is documented in docs/reference/mcp/state.md and docs/reference/gs/state.md; no UI code is touched, Codex owns forms and display. Original acceptance (unchanged at this head) executes actual CLI, MCP and HTTP filings and inspects stored schema and folded result: cmd/gs/request_authoring_test.go, cmd/gitseq-mcp/request_authoring_test.go, internal/service/request_authoring_test.go cover by-value, inherit, no-artifact and held, the refusal table with unchanged-frontier assertions, ref movement with exact accepted retry, legacy state@2 replay and both reassignment cases. Guards proved by removal, each red on the named test and restored: caller target_repo/target_head refusal, branch-shape check, unresolvable-ref refusal, shared choice judgement and hold rule (TestCLIRequestRefusesBeforeAnyAppend); state@3 signing (TestCLIRequestStatesItsResult, schema reads state@2); reassign@1 schema, fold reading and own choice (TestCLIReassignmentStatesTheReplacementResult); accepted-act reproduction (TestCLIRequestMeasuresTheRefAtEachFiling, idempotency key reused with different intent); MCP and resident surfaces (TestMCPRequestStatesItsResult, TestResidentRequestStatesItsResult). I re-ran four of these whole-guard mutants myself in a separate detached worktree at this head with the same red lines. Gates at this exact head: gofmt clean, git diff --check clean, go vet clean, go build clean, go test -race -count=1 on internal/workroom, internal/app, internal/mergeplan, internal/service, internal/kernel, cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp all ok, go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 with all 35 packages ok, GOFLAGS=-count=1 make docs ok. Architecture: layers 3 (kernel), 4 (intent), 5 (workroom fold and profile), 6 (app) and 7 (surfaces) change contract; docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in this head. Security: caller intent is compared and never rewritten during replay; only server-derived measurement is recovered, under the caller's own key from the same verified frontier Submit consults; a legacy act is reproduced only under its own accepted schema and only on byte equality, so no fresh request bypasses the required choice; a replacement is judged before the retirement so invalid caller input cannot withdraw an assignment; the profile advance keeps the cache interpretation boundary honest. Simplification: one shared preflight/replay path (guardedReplacementBody, acceptedRequestReproduction) and the existing append guards; no retry cache or second state machine; examples teach the real result choice. Reviewer note: the widened gate costs one PriorAct scan per keyed request filing. Branch pushed to origin; worktree retained until merge.","body":{"commit":"21b7e74225885452ab0ad0dc49b33aaf2c326d54","path":"internal/app/request_authoring.go"}}